            "dct:description": {
                "@language": "eng",
                "@value": "The datasets in this database provide long-term hydro-climatological information for Luxembourg, monitored and managed by the Luxembourg Eco-hydrological Observatory (LEO) platform of the Luxembourg Institute of Science and Technology (LIST).\nData are updated regularly; Therefore, please take note of the creation date of each dataset. The data tables include Quality Control (QC) codes indicating validation status, which may be revised over time.\nIn addition to LEO data, the datasets also integrate contributions from national public agencies, including the Administration de la Gestion de l’Eau (AGE), the Administration des Services Techniques de l’Agriculture (ASTA), and MeteoLux."
            },
            "dct:accessRights": {
